Keep Android vendor libraries mapped until process-worker ring threads finish.

Android Vulkan HALs can register Bionic thread-local destructors in libraries
that the loader unloads during vkDestroyInstance.  A Venus ring thread then
calls an unmapped destructor while exiting.  Each process worker serves one
guest VkInstance connection, so let worker process exit reclaim the native
instance while retaining explicit destruction for thread workers.

diff --git a/src/venus/vkr_instance.c b/src/venus/vkr_instance.c
index a5002a35..e1681bda 100644
--- a/src/venus/vkr_instance.c
+++ b/src/venus/vkr_instance.c
@@ -279,7 +279,15 @@ vkr_dispatch_vkDestroyInstance(struct vn_dispatch_context *dispatch,
       return;
    }
 
-   vkr_instance_destroy(ctx, instance, true);
+#ifdef __ANDROID__
+   /* A process worker exits when this instance's vtest connection closes.  Let
+    * process teardown release the native instance so Android vendor libraries
+    * remain mapped until their Bionic thread-local destructors have run. */
+   const bool destroy_vk = ctx->on_worker_thread;
+#else
+   const bool destroy_vk = true;
+#endif
+   vkr_instance_destroy(ctx, instance, destroy_vk);
 }
 
 void
